c method.\n\nAlternatively, the user might have made a mistake in the guidelines. But since the user says "you must conform to these essential guidelines," I have to follow them.\n\nSo, perhaps the solution is:\n\nclass VolumeCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def volume_cuboid(length, width, height):\n        return int(length * width * height)\n\nThis way, the function is a static method of the class, and it takes the three parameters. The class encapsulates the behavior. This satisfies the guideline of encapsulating into a class and the single responsibility principle.\n\nAdditionally, the function is concise (only 1 line after the method definition), so it\'s under 10 lines.\n\nNow, checking the other guidelines: Single Responsibility Principle. The function has one responsibility: calculating the volume. So that\'s satisfied.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be a class with a static method volume_cuboid as above.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\n# experiments/solution.py\nclass VolumeCalculator:\n    @staticmethod\n    def volume_cuboid(length, width, height):\n        return int(length * width * height)\n</answer>'
