ll the requirements. The type hints are present, the function name is correct, and it returns the product of base and height as an integer.\n\nI should check if there are any other considerations. The problem says to prioritize type safety and explicitness. The code does that by specifying the types for parameters and return value. The mypy check should pass without errors.\n\nYes, this should be the correct solution.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\n```python\n# experiments/solution.py\n\ndef parallelogram_area(base: int, height: int) -> int:\n    """\n    Calculate the area of a parallelogram given its base and height.\n    \n    Args:\n        base: The base length of the parallelogram as an integer.\n        height: The height of the parallelogram as an integer.\n        \n    Returns:\n        The area of the parallelogram as an integer.\n    """\n    return base * height\n```\n</answer>'
