he replace operation.\n\nI think this meets all the guidelines: type hints, docstring, and encapsulation in a function. There\'s not much complexity here, so unpacking into intermediate variables isn\'t necessary. The code is concise and readable.\n\nNow, I need to place this in experiments/solution.py. The user\'s current directory is /root/qwen3_rl_training, so the file path would be experiments/solution.py.\n\nSo the script would be the function as written above. I need to make sure that the code is properly formatted and saved in the correct file.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\n```python\n# experiments/solution.py\n\ndef remove_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    """\n    Removes all spaces from the input string.\n    \n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string from which spaces will be removed.\n        \n    Returns:\n        str: A new string with all spaces removed.\n        \n    Example:\n        >>> remove_spaces("Hello world!")\n        \'Helloworld!\'\n    """\n    # Create a copy of the input string with all space characters (\' \') removed\n    # The str.replace() method is used to substitute spaces with an empty string\n    return input_string.replace(" ", "")\n```\n</answer>'
