ode would be:\n\ndef minimum(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    return min(x, y)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    print(minimum(3, 5))  # Output: 3\n    print(minimum(-1, 0))  # Output: -1\n\nThat should meet all the requirements. The function is correct, the main block has tests, and no constants are needed. The file is saved properly. I think that's all.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\ndef minimum(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n    return min(x, y)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    print(minimum(3, 5))\n    print(minimum(-1, 0))\n</answer>"
