ed to create that as well.\n\nBut the user's current directory structure has experiments with problem.txt, and the output.log and run.sh. The user hasn't mentioned any existing tests, so adding a test file is necessary.\n\nSo the steps are: create experiments/solution.py with the function, and experiments/test_solution.py with the unit tests.\n\nNow, the unit tests. Using something like pytest. For example:\n\nimport pytest\nfrom experiments.solution import first_odd\n\ndef test_first_odd():\n    assert first_odd([2,4,6]) is None\n    assert first_odd([3,2,4]) == 3\n    assert first_odd([4,5,6]) ==5\n    assert first_odd([]) is None\n    assert first_odd([0, -1, 2]) == -1\n    assert first_odd([1,3,5]) ==1\n\nBut the problem says to put the code in experiments/solution.py, so the tests would go into another file. Since the user didn't have a test file, I need to create that as part of the solution.\n\nHowever, in the initial problem statement, the user only requires placing the code in experiments/solution.py. The unit test is part of the specifications the user provided as an engineer. So, the answer must include the code for the function and the unit test.\n\nBut the user's instruction says to place the final code in experiments/solution.py. The user might expect that the test is written in a separate file. Therefore, the answer includes the function in solution.py and the test in test_solution.py.\n\nTherefore, the final answer will have the function in experiments/solution.py and the tests in experiments/test_solution.py.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\n### experiments/solution.py ###\ndef first_odd(numbers):\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num % 2 != 0:\n            return num\n    return None\n\n### experiments/test_solution.py ###\nimport pytest\nfrom experiments.solution import first_odd\n\ndef test_first_odd():\n    assert first_odd([2,4,6]) is None\n    assert first_odd([3,2,4]) == 3\n    assert first_odd([4,5,6]) == 5\n    assert first_odd([]) is None\n    as