as given, and adheres to the company\'s rules by using the correct operators and structure.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\n```python\n# experiments/solution.py\n\ndef perimeter_triangle(a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\n    """\n    Calculate the perimeter of a triangle given its three sides.\n    \n    Args:\n        a: Length of side a (integer)\n        b: Length of side b (integer)\n        c: Length of side c (integer)\n        \n    Returns:\n        Integer representing the perimeter (a + b + c)\n    """\n    return a + b + c\n```\n</answer>'
