user wants the solution placed in experiments/solution.py. So the code will be in that file.\n\nTesting the code: when someone runs the script with the arguments, it should compute the profit or return None as specified.\n\nNow, code structure:\n\nImport argparse.\n\nDefine the function.\n\nParse arguments.\n\nCall the function with the parsed values.\n\nPrint the result.\n\nAlso, include the version in the code, maybe using a __version__ variable.\n\nBut the problem says the version number of the project should follow Semantic Versioning. So maybe the script should print the version when run with --version, but the problem might not require that. The exact requirement is that the version number is in the project, so perhaps just define __version__ = "1.0.0" in the code.\n\nThe README should be updated with instructions. So in the experiments directory, create a README.md that explains how to run the solution.py script.\n\nSo in the solution, the code will be:\n\nIn experiments/solution.py:\n\nimport argparse\n\ndef profit_amount(selling_price, cost_price):\n    if selling_price > cost_price:\n        return selling_price - cost_price\n    else:\n        return None\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Calculate profit amount.")\n    parser.add_argument("--selling-price", type=float, required=True, help="The selling price.")\n    parser.add_argument("--cost-price", type=float, required=True, help="The cost price.")\n    parser.add_argument("--version", action="version", version="%(prog)s 1.0.0")\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    result = profit_amount(args.selling_price, args.cost_price)\n    print("Profit:", result)\n\nThen, the README.md in the experiments directory would have:\n\n# Solution for Profit Calculation\n\n## Description\nThis script calculates the profit amount based on the given selling price and cost price.\n\n## Usage\nTo run the script, use the following command:\n\n```bash\npython solution.py --selling-price <price> --cost-price <price>\n```\n\nReplace `<price>` with the actual numerical values for selling and cost prices.\n\nFor version information:\n\n```bash\npython solution.py --version\n```\n\nThis will display the current version of the script.\n\nThat should cover all the requirements. The code handles the command-line arguments with argparse, includes a version number, and the README explains how to run it.\n</think>\n\n<answer>\nHere\'s the solution:\n\n```python\n# experiments/solution.py\nimport argparse\n\n__version__ = "1.0.0"\n\ndef profit_amount(selling_price, cost_price):\n    """\n    Calculate the profit amount if selling price is greater than cost price.\n    \n    Args:\n        selling_price (float): The price at which the item is sold.\n        cost_price (float): The original cost of the item.\n        \n    Returns:\n        float or None: The profit amount if selling price > cost price, otherwise None.\n    """\n    if selling_price > cost_price:\n        return selling_price - cost_price\n    return None\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description="Profit calculation tool")\n    parser.add_argument("--selling-price", type=float, required=True, help="The selling price of the item")\n    parser.add_argument("--cost-price", type=float, required=True, help="The cost price of the item")\n    parser.add_argument("--version", action="version", version=f"%(prog)s {__version__}", help="Show version information")\n    \n    args = parser.parse_args()\n    result = profit_amount(args.selling_price, args.cost_price)\n    print(f"Profit: {result}")\n```\n\nThe README.md file should contain:\n\n```\n# Profit Calculation Solution\n\n## Description\nThis script calculates the profit amount when the selling price exceeds the cost price.\n\n## Usage\nRun the script with the following command:\n\n```bash\npython solution.py --selling-price <value> --cost-price <value>\n```\n\nReplace `<value>` with numerical values for the selling and cost prices.\n\n## Version\nThe current version is 1.0.0. Check the version with:\n\n```bash\npython solution.py --version\n```\n```\n\n</answer>'
